  ($seed$aeronautical_engineer$seed$, $seed$aviation_aerospace$seed$, $seed$Aeronautical Engineer$seed$, $seed$Aeronautical Eng.$seed$, $seed$aeronautical-engineer$seed$, $seed$Focuses on aircraft that operate within Earth's atmosphere, covering flight mechanics, aerodynamics, and airframe design.$seed$, $seed$Analyzes how an aircraft's shape, weight, and control surfaces affect its flight behavior, working on aerodynamics, stability, and airframe design specifically for atmospheric flight. Runs computational fluid dynamics simulations and reviews flight-test data to refine designs. Often works alongside structural, avionics, and manufacturing teams on a specific aircraft program.$seed$, $seed$Design-office and simulation work for most of the week, with scheduled time at wind tunnels or flight-test sites, typically as part of a larger aircraft program team.$seed$, null, $seed$Junior aerodynamics or design engineer at an aircraft manufacturer or aviation research lab$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 4, 1, 1, 4, 4, 3, 3, 3, 2, 4, 5, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
