  ($seed$aircraft_maintenance_engineer$seed$, $seed$aviation_aerospace$seed$, $seed$Aircraft Maintenance Engineer$seed$, $seed$AME$seed$, $seed$aircraft-maintenance-engineer$seed$, $seed$Inspects, maintains, and certifies aircraft as airworthy under strict regulatory standards.$seed$, $seed$Carries out scheduled inspections, repairs, and component replacements on aircraft, following manufacturer manuals and aviation authority regulations. Diagnoses faults in mechanical, electrical, and avionics systems, signs off maintenance records, and certifies aircraft as fit to fly. Work is hands-on and documentation-heavy, since every task must be traceable and auditable.$seed$, $seed$Hangar and airside work on aircraft, often in shifts to match flight schedules, as part of a maintenance crew reporting to a certifying engineer or maintenance manager.$seed$, null, $seed$Licensed or trainee aircraft maintenance engineer at an airline, MRO facility, or defense unit$seed$, $seed$diploma$seed$, 4, 1, 1, 3, 4, 1, 3, 3, 2, 1, 4, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
