  ($seed$geologist$seed$, $seed$physical_sciences$seed$, $seed$Geologist$seed$, null, $seed$geologist$seed$, $seed$Studies the physical structure and history of the Earth, investigating rocks, minerals, and geological processes for resource, hazard, or research purposes.$seed$, $seed$Conducts field surveys to map rock formations and collect samples, analyzes geological data to locate resources such as minerals, groundwater, or oil and gas, and assesses risks like landslides or earthquakes. Splits time between field expeditions and lab or office-based analysis and reporting.$seed$, $seed$A mix of remote or rugged field sites and office/lab-based analysis, often for mining, oil and gas, construction, or government geological survey organizations.$seed$, null, $seed$Junior/field geologist at a mining, oil and gas, or geotechnical consulting firm$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 4, 1, 2, 3, 3, 2, 3, 2, 5, 3, 4, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$architect$seed$, $seed$architecture_built_environment$seed$, $seed$Architect$seed$, null, $seed$architect$seed$, $seed$Designs buildings and spaces, balancing function, safety, aesthetics, and budget from concept through construction.$seed$, $seed$Develops design concepts, drafts technical drawings and building plans, and coordinates with structural and services engineers so a design is buildable and code-compliant. Presents concepts to clients, prepares documents for regulatory approval, and visits sites during construction to check that what gets built matches the design intent.$seed$, $seed$Split between studio or office design work and periodic site visits during construction, usually within a small-to-mid-sized architecture practice or a larger multidisciplinary design firm.$seed$, null, $seed$Junior architect or architectural assistant working under a registered architect$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 4, 2, 3, 3, 3, 5, 4, 3, 3, 2, 4, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$urban_planner$seed$, $seed$architecture_built_environment$seed$, $seed$Urban Planner$seed$, null, $seed$urban-planner$seed$, $seed$Prepares land-use plans and policy recommendations that guide how towns and cities grow, balancing development, infrastructure, and community needs.$seed$, $seed$Analyzes population, transport, and land-use data to draft zoning and development plans, and works with local government, developers, and residents to shape how land gets used. Reviews development proposals against planning regulations and prepares reports and presentations for public consultations and council approvals.$seed$, $seed$Primarily office-based work within a municipal planning department or a private planning consultancy, with periodic site visits and public meetings.$seed$, null, $seed$Graduate or assistant planner in a municipal planning department or planning consultancy$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 3, 2, 2, 3, 4, 3, 5, 3, 2, 4, 3, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$ux_designer$seed$, $seed$design_creative$seed$, $seed$UX Designer$seed$, null, $seed$ux-designer$seed$, $seed$Researches how people use digital products and designs the flows, structure, and interactions that make software easy and effective to use.$seed$, $seed$Conducts user research and usability testing, maps user journeys and information architecture, and designs wireframes and interactive prototypes for websites and apps. Works closely with product managers and UI designers to turn research findings into design decisions, and revises designs based on testing feedback.$seed$, $seed$Mostly computer-based work within a product or design team, often collaborating across product, engineering, and research functions, sometimes remotely.$seed$, null, $seed$Junior or associate UX designer, or UX research assistant, on a product, tech, or digital agency team$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 4, 5, 3, 4, 3, 4, 3, 3, 1, 4, 3, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$ui_designer$seed$, $seed$design_creative$seed$, $seed$UI Designer$seed$, null, $seed$ui-designer$seed$, $seed$Designs the visual look and detailed interface elements of digital products, defining layout, typography, color, and interactive components.$seed$, $seed$Turns wireframes and UX flows into polished visual interfaces, and builds and maintains component libraries and design systems. Chooses typography, color palettes, iconography, and micro-interactions, and works closely with UX designers and front-end developers to keep the shipped product consistent with the design.$seed$, $seed$Computer-based work within a product or design team, usually alongside UX designers, engineers, and product managers.$seed$, null, $seed$Junior UI designer or visual designer on a digital product or design team$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 4, 5, 3, 3, 3, 5, 2, 2, 1, 2, 3, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$product_designer$seed$, $seed$design_creative$seed$, $seed$Product Designer$seed$, null, $seed$product-designer$seed$, $seed$Owns the end-to-end design of a digital product, combining user research, interaction design, and visual design to shape what gets built.$seed$, $seed$Works across the full design process — research, journey mapping, wireframing, visual design, and prototyping — while partnering closely with product managers and engineers on what gets built and why. Presents design rationale to stakeholders and makes trade-off calls between user needs, business goals, and technical constraints.$seed$, $seed$Embedded within a cross-functional product team, mixing independent design work with frequent collaboration, reviews, and stakeholder meetings.$seed$, null, $seed$Product designer on a startup or established product team, often after starting as a UX or UI designer$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 4, 4, 4, 4, 3, 4, 3, 4, 1, 3, 3, true, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$graphic_designer$seed$, $seed$design_creative$seed$, $seed$Graphic Designer$seed$, null, $seed$graphic-designer$seed$, $seed$Creates visual content — branding, marketing materials, layouts, and print or digital graphics — for businesses, agencies, or publications.$seed$, $seed$Designs logos, brand identity assets, marketing collateral, packaging, and layouts for print and digital use, working from client or brand briefs. Selects typography, imagery, and color schemes, and prepares final files for print production or digital publishing.$seed$, $seed$Studio or office-based work at a design agency, in-house marketing team, or as a freelancer, often juggling several client projects and deadlines at once.$seed$, null, $seed$Junior graphic designer at a design studio, agency, or in-house marketing/creative team$seed$, $seed$diploma$seed$, 3, 4, 4, 2, 2, 5, 2, 2, 1, 1, 2, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$industrial_designer$seed$, $seed$design_creative$seed$, $seed$Industrial Designer$seed$, null, $seed$industrial-designer$seed$, $seed$Designs the form, function, and usability of physical products, from consumer electronics to furniture, balancing aesthetics with manufacturability.$seed$, $seed$Sketches and models product concepts and uses CAD software to refine form, ergonomics, and materials before a product goes into manufacturing. Builds and tests prototypes, and works with engineers and manufacturers to make sure a design can actually be produced at the intended cost and quality.$seed$, $seed$A mix of studio design work, CAD and prototyping labs, and factory or workshop visits, usually within a product design consultancy or an in-house design team at a manufacturer.$seed$, null, $seed$Junior industrial or product designer at a design consultancy or manufacturing company$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 4, 2, 3, 3, 3, 5, 3, 3, 2, 3, 4, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$lawyer$seed$, $seed$law_legal$seed$, $seed$Lawyer$seed$, $seed$Lawyer$seed$, $seed$lawyer$seed$, $seed$Advises clients on legal matters and represents them in disputes, contracts, and court proceedings across civil, criminal, or specialized practice areas.$seed$, $seed$Researches statutes and case law, drafts legal documents such as contracts and pleadings, and advises individuals or organizations on their rights and obligations. Represents clients in negotiations, tribunals, or court, and prepares arguments and evidence for cases. Work often splits between a general practice covering multiple areas of law or a focused specialization such as criminal, family, or property law.$seed$, $seed$Works from a law office or chambers, with regular time in courtrooms, client meetings, and tribunals; often part of a small partnership or works independently after gaining experience under a senior advocate.$seed$, null, $seed$Junior associate or apprentice under a practicing advocate after qualifying to practice law$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 2, 2, 3, 4, 3, null, 3, 3, null, 3, 3, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$corporate_lawyer$seed$, $seed$law_legal$seed$, $seed$Corporate Lawyer$seed$, $seed$Corporate Lawyer$seed$, $seed$corporate-lawyer$seed$, $seed$Handles the legal side of business transactions such as mergers, contracts, and regulatory compliance for companies and financial institutions.$seed$, $seed$Drafts and reviews commercial contracts, structures mergers and acquisitions, and advises companies on regulatory compliance, corporate governance, and risk. Works closely with finance and business teams during deals, due diligence, and negotiations, often under tight transaction deadlines. Typically practices within a law firm's corporate/M&A team or an in-house legal department.$seed$, $seed$Office-based work at a corporate law firm or in-house legal team, with long hours around deal closings and heavy coordination with bankers, executives, and other lawyers.$seed$, null, $seed$Associate in a corporate/M&A practice group at a law firm, or junior counsel in an in-house legal team$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 4, 2, 2, 5, 4, null, 2, 4, null, 3, 3, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$civil_services_officer$seed$, $seed$government_public_policy$seed$, $seed$Civil Services Officer (Public Administration)$seed$, $seed$Civil Services Officer$seed$, $seed$civil-services-officer$seed$, $seed$Administers government policy and public services at the district, state, or national level after qualifying through a competitive civil services examination.$seed$, $seed$Implements government policy on the ground, manages public administration for a district or department, and oversees law and order, welfare schemes, or revenue administration depending on the posting. Coordinates between elected representatives, government departments, and the public, and makes decisions that affect large numbers of people. Postings rotate across departments and regions over a career, with increasing responsibility over time.$seed$, $seed$Government offices and field visits within an assigned district or department, with regular public interaction, inter-departmental coordination, and periodic transfers to new postings.$seed$, null, $seed$Probationary officer after clearing a national or state civil services examination$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 2, 1, 1, 3, 5, null, 5, 5, 3, null, 2, true, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$policy_analyst$seed$, $seed$government_public_policy$seed$, $seed$Policy Analyst$seed$, $seed$Policy Analyst$seed$, $seed$policy-analyst$seed$, $seed$Researches issues, evaluates options, and writes recommendations that inform government, think-tank, or NGO decisions on public policy.$seed$, $seed$Studies a policy area such as education, health, or urban planning, gathers data and stakeholder input, and compares the likely effects of different policy options. Writes briefing papers, reports, and recommendations for decision-makers, and sometimes presents findings to government committees or the public. Work varies with employer, from a government ministry to a think tank, research institute, or advocacy organization.$seed$, $seed$Primarily office-based research and writing, with periodic stakeholder meetings, field data collection, or committee presentations; usually part of a small research or policy team.$seed$, null, $seed$Research associate or junior policy analyst at a think tank, government department, or NGO$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 3, 3, 2, 3, 3, null, 4, 2, null, 5, 2, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$teacher$seed$, $seed$education$seed$, $seed$Teacher$seed$, $seed$Teacher$seed$, $seed$teacher$seed$, $seed$Plans and delivers lessons to school students, assesses their learning, and supports their academic and personal development.$seed$, $seed$Plans lessons aligned to a curriculum, teaches classes, sets and grades assignments and exams, and tracks each student's progress. Manages classroom behavior, communicates with parents, and often takes on additional duties such as coaching a club, organizing events, or mentoring students individually. Subject and grade level vary widely, from primary school generalist teaching to subject-specialist secondary school teaching.$seed$, $seed$Classroom-based work in a school, with lesson planning and grading done outside class hours; involves regular collaboration with other teachers and periodic parent meetings.$seed$, null, $seed$Assistant or probationary teacher in a school after completing a teaching qualification$seed$, $seed$bachelors$seed$, 2, 1, 1, 2, 4, 3, 5, 2, null, null, 2, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$professor$seed$, $seed$education$seed$, $seed$Professor$seed$, $seed$Professor$seed$, $seed$professor$seed$, $seed$Teaches at the college or university level and conducts original research within an academic discipline, publishing findings for the field.$seed$, $seed$Teaches undergraduate or graduate courses, mentors research students, and conducts original research culminating in publications, grant proposals, or conference presentations. Balances time between lecturing, grading, committee and administrative work, and independent or collaborative research. Career progression typically moves from a postdoctoral or assistant professor role toward tenure and more senior academic positions.$seed$, $seed$University campus work split between lecture halls, research labs or offices, and academic conferences, with substantial independent, self-directed time for research and writing.$seed$, null, $seed$Postdoctoral researcher or assistant professor after completing a doctoral degree$seed$, $seed$phd$seed$, 4, 2, 1, 3, 4, 3, 3, 3, null, 5, 4, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$psychologist$seed$, $seed$psychology_human_services$seed$, $seed$Psychologist$seed$, $seed$Psychologist$seed$, $seed$psychologist$seed$, $seed$Assesses and treats mental health and behavioral concerns using psychological theory and evidence-based therapeutic techniques.$seed$, $seed$Conducts assessments and interviews to understand a client's psychological concerns, applies therapeutic techniques such as cognitive-behavioral therapy, and tracks progress over a course of treatment. Maintains detailed case notes, may administer standardized psychological tests, and refers clients to psychiatrists or other specialists when needed. Some psychologists focus on clinical practice while others work in research, organizational, or educational settings.$seed$, $seed$One-on-one or group sessions in a clinic, hospital, school, or private practice, with significant time spent on case documentation and, for some roles, supervision or research.$seed$, null, $seed$Supervised clinical trainee or assistant psychologist after completing a relevant postgraduate degree$seed$, $seed$masters$seed$, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 2, 5, null, null, 3, 3, false, $seed$approved$seed$),
  ($seed$counselor$seed$, $seed$psychology_human_services$seed$, $seed$Counselor$seed$, $seed$Counselor$seed$, $seed$counselor$seed$, $seed$Guides individuals or groups through personal, academic, or career challenges using structured conversation, active listening, and practical support.$seed$, $seed$Meets with clients individually or in groups to talk through personal, academic, or career-related difficulties, and helps them work toward practical next steps. Common settings include school career counseling, academic guidance, or general life-skills counseling, each with a somewhat different focus. Keeps confidential records of sessions and refers clients to a psychologist or other specialist when concerns go beyond the counselor's scope.$seed$, $seed$Office-based one-on-one or group sessions in a school, college, or community setting, with a steady, appointment-driven schedule and regular coordination with teachers, parents, or other staff.$seed$, null, $seed$School or college counselor after completing a relevant postgraduate qualification in counseling or psychology$seed$, $seed$masters$seed$, 1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 2, 5, null, null, null, 2, false, $seed$approved$seed$)
